    "background_story": "Julian was a renowned botanist with a passion for rare and exotic plants. His life's work was dedicated to studying the Erigeron, a genus of flowering plants commonly known as fleabanes. Julian spent years traveling the world, from the mountains of Japan to the deserts of North America, in search of new species to add to his collection. His most notable discovery was the Erigeron julianus, a previously unknown variety found in the remote regions of the Andes. The plant's unique properties made it a valuable find, with potential applications in medicine and conservation. Julian's dedication to his craft earned him the respect of his peers, and his discovery of the Erigeron julianus cemented his legacy as one of the greatest botanists of his time.",
